ence_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2 and 3; Figure 2b caption: BRAN monthly climatology, density-layer context and approximate 60-105 E reach shifting from 8 S to 10 S. Figure 3 core threshold is a separate diagnostic.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Chen, Han, Zu, Chu and Chen (2022), The Deep-Penetrating South Equatorial Undercurrent in the Tropical South Indian Ocean, Geophysical Research Letters 49, e2022GL098163, doi:10.1029/2022GL098163.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Attributed factual geography; no source figure, velocity field or model array copied. No open figure-reuse license inferred.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Rounded 60 E, 8 S and 105 E, 10 S follow approximate prose context. OSW interpolates middle vertices; no dotted core center or bathymetric contour traced. Alternative middle latitude bends and endpoint shifts test editorial drawing choices, not source position errors.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      60,\r\n      -8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      70,\r\n      -8.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      80,\r\n      -9\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      90,\r\n      -9.5\r\n   