 \"Deep Western Boundary Current\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"North Atlantic study-section reach from 47 degrees N to 24.5 degrees N via a coarse western-boundary reference corridor. Excludes upstream subpolar circulation, interior pathways, recirculation and tropical/South Atlantic continuation. Not the whole DWBC or a continuous observed deep-water pathway.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Source-defined deep circulation: around 2800 m to bottom at 47 degrees N, around 2682 m to bottom at 36 degrees N, and around 2500–5500 m at 24.5 degrees N. Interfaces vary by section; no common fixed-depth axis reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route linking source section latitudes; not a simultaneous measured trajectory or a 1990–2019 mean current axis.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.2.3 and Figure 8/Table 3: DWBC sections at 47, 36 and 24.5 degrees N, section-specific deep interfaces and western Atlantic boundary geography. Section widths are not along-current lengths.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Caínzos et al. (2023), Consistent picture of the horizontal circulation of the Atlantic Ocean over 3 decades, Ocean Science 19, 1009–1045.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Factual geographic references only; no source prose, figures, provider geometry or model data packaged.\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore waypoints from the Grand Banks region toward the Bahamas. Source section locations constrain latitude and deep-flow identity; these intermediate coordinates are not published axes or diagnosed bathymetric contours. Continuity between sections remains an assumption.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -44.5,\r\n      47\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -47,\r\n      43\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -52,\r\n      41\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -62,\r\n      39\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -70,\r\n      36\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -74,\r\n      32\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -76,\r\n      28\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -75,\r\n      24.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three uniform longitude offsets (-0.5/0/+0.5 degrees) crossed with three independent endpoint latitude offsets (-0.5/0/+0.5 degrees): 27 editorial scenarios. This limited corridor sensitivity does not encompass interior pathways or establish a continuous observed current.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Independent scientific review of the chosen boundary corridor, section joins and interior pathway alternatives.\",\r\n    \"Validate deep route with bathymetry and layer-specific velocity geometry; coarse surface-land clearance is insufficient.\",\r\n    \"Keep study reach excluded from whole-current ordering; canonical integration and publication review required.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    470,\r\n    205,\r\n    210,\r\n    195\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"47°N study gate\",\r\n    \"24.5°N study gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Caínzos et al. (2023), §3.2.3\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Atlantic studied reach\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-02\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"a969c28dc97266982bd61f472433f1f63d24644ad8e6d5a76dba8b13c367a934\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WG