/doi/full/10.1029/2008GL035753\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 2 [6]–[7] and Fig. 1: floats parked at 200 m; 174 ten-day zonal-flow estimates within 3–6 S, 35 W to approximately 10 W. Section 4 [9]: mean core around 3 S at 35 W and slightly south of 4 S farther east. Sections 5–6: western meanders and unresolved layer-dependent connectivity.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Fischer, Hormann, Brandt, Schott, Rabe and Funk (2008), South Equatorial Undercurrent in the western to central tropical Atlantic, Geophysical Research Letters 35, doi:10.1029/2008GL035753.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Publisher free-access article, no open reuse license inferred. Attributed regional facts paraphrased; no figures, float curves or observed fields copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects rounded waypoints between the source section and float-domain longitudes, using the mean-core latitude context around 3 S at 35 W and slightly south of 4 S eastward. The 10 W latitude is editorial. Smooth bends test a regional reference path, not the documented western standing-wave shape, individual float excursions or recirculation. No source trajectory or velocity contour digitized.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -35,\r\n      -3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -32,\r\n      -4.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -28,\r\n      -4.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -23,\r\n      -4.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -17,\r\n      -4.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -10,\r\n      -4.3\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_reference_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          -3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -32,\r\n          -4.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -28,\r\n          -4.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -23,\r\n          -4.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -17,\r\n          -4.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -10.5,\r\n          -4.1\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW northern smooth reference bend with an earlier study truncation; not an observed seasonal axis or width edge.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_reference_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          -3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -32,\r\n          -4.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -28,\r\n          -4.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -23,\r\n          -4.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -17,\r\n          -4.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -9.5,\r\n          -4.8\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW southern smooth bend and later study truncation; no individual float loop or actual western standing wave reconstructed.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared reach shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees: 81 editorial cases, not physical width, seasonal variation or statistical confidence.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review gates, western meanders and chosen core-latitude smoothing with compatible velocity or trajectory data.\",\r\n    \"Resolve the eastern rise and fate before whole-current endpoints; 10 W is study truncation.\",\r\n    \"Separate 200 m float sampling from ship-section depth/density transport definitions and surface drift.\",\r\n    \"Diagnose paired lateral boundaries before width; 3–6 S is a sampling band, not full-current width.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    620,\r\n    405,\r\n    190,\r\n    150\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 2.7,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 4.5,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.65,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"35 W section context\",\r\n    \"10 W study truncation\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Fischer et al. (2008), sec. 2 and 4\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"200 m context western-to-central studied reach\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"3bddf4fad1bd02b983c05538acc7428dbea21ed8101f7cfc1510467e2c1f4150\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 2805.134,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 2800,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2733.554,\r\n    2899.58\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2700,\r\n    2900\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -35.25,\r\n          -3.25\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -32.25,\r\n          -4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -28.25,\r\n          -4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -23.25,\r\n          -4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -17.25,\r\n          -4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -10.25,\r\n          -4.55\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"length_km\": 2795.42,\r\n      \"atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"ETRA\",\r\n        \"WTRA\"