081698e98","source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Publisher PDF states CC Attribution 3.0. No source figures, trajectories or velocity grids packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    0\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.05,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 1.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.45,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review the whole circuit against bathymetry and compatible geostrophic velocity geometry; no observed axis reconstructed.\",\r\n    \"Resolve seasonal continuity and distinguish connected circuit from summer-fall eddy fragmentation before annual geometry claims.\",\r\n    \"Keep interior/coastal gyres and historical sector names distinct from the main circuit; no branch/eddy lengths added.\",\r\n    \"Do not convert northern/southern intensity-index monitoring windows into full-current dimensions.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"black-sea-rim\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Black Sea Rim Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"One declared counterclockwise Black Sea basin-margin reference circuit under the surface geostrophic circulation convention. An arbitrary western anchor closes the path; it is not a current origin or termination. Excludes the interior Western/Eastern gyres, coastal eddy loops and branch sums. Historical Caucasus and Southern Current naming equivalence remains unresolved.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Surface geostrophic circulation context; source drifters have mixed near-surface support through the first 15 m, with wind-driven components estimated separately. No uniform full-depth axis inferred.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial closed-circuit geography in the context of the source 1999-2009 surface geostrophic statistics. Vertices are not extracted from the mean field or any dated frame. Closure does not establish continuous seasonal flow, parcel circulation time or annual extrema.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/10/155/2014/os-10-155-2014.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Introduction; Section 2; Sections 3.1 and 3.2.1: surface geostrophic context, seasonal anomalies and Rim circuit around interior gyres.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Menna and Poulain (2014), Geostrophic currents and kinetic energies in the Black Sea estimated from merged drifter and satellite altimetry data, Ocean Science 10, 155-165, doi:10.5194/os-10-155-2014.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore vertices around the Anatolian, Caucasus and Crimean basin-margin neighborhoods. The northern path skirts south of Crimea and omits interior gyre circuits. Alternatives vary detour shape without tracing source velocity arrows or a particular isobath. No source field digitized. Closed path length counts every leg once, including the closing leg. A declared offshore bend around the Sinop coastal protrusion prevents a straight southern chord crossing the coarse land shape; the bend is not a measured jet meander.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      29,\r\n      42.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      29.5,\r\n      41.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      32,\r\n      41.85\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      35,\r\n      42.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      38,\r\n      41.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      40.5,\r\n      42.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      40.25,\r\n      43\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      38.3,\r\n      43.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      36.5,\r\n      44\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      34.3,\r\n      43.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      32,\r\n      43.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      30,\r\n      43\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      29,\r\n      42.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"inner_reference_circuit\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          29.3,\r\n          42.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          29.8,\r\n          42.05\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          32,\r\n          42.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          35,\r\n          42.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          38,\r\n          42.05\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          40.1,\r\n          42.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          40,\r\n          42.9\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          38.3,\r\n          43.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          36.5,\r\n          43.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          34.3,\r\n          43.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          32,\r\n          43.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          30.3,\r\n          42.9\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          29.3,\r\n          42.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"More interior editorial circuit with shorter peripheral detours; not a seasonal flow or inner current edge.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"outer_reference_circuit\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          28.85,\r\n          42.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          29.4,\r\n          41.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          32,\r\n          41.95\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          35,\r\n          42.35\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          38,\r\n          41.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          40.7,\r\n          42.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          40.2,\r\n          43\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          38.3,\r\n          43.75\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          36.5,\r\n          44.15\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          34.3,\r\n          43.75\r\