l kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_D_2\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/black-sea-rim-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n"},"research/east-australian-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_sha256":"f9e903221cf97d197e7b6f2f62094fd6bd7d99fe82d852af857b1f54e31a20d8","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"east-australian\",\r\n  \"name\": \"East Australian Current\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Coherent poleward shelf-break jet from about 15 degrees S to the usual separation around 32 degrees S; excludes Tasman Front and downstream eddy/extension routes.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Jet geographic description; no velocity layer or depth integration diagnosed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"General geographic reference sketch; not the instantaneous model surface-speed snapshot in Figure 1 or a dated observed centerline.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/3853/2026/\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1 Introduction, opening paragraph (15 degrees S to usual separation around 32 degrees S); Figure 1 for regional orientation only.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Reilly et al. (2026), Two-tier MOM6 regional modelling suite of the East Australian Current system, Geoscientific Model Development 19, 3853-3873, doi:10.5194/gmd-19-3853-2026.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"CC BY 4.0\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW chooses coarse offshore waypoints to sketch the east Australian shelf-break corridor. The source supplies latitude limits and flow description, not these longitudes, intermediate vertices, or a numerical current length. These vertices are not digitized model data or published coordinates.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      147.5,\r\n      -15\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      149.5,\r\n      -18\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      152.5,\r\n      -21\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      154,\r\n      -24\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      154,\r\n      -27\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      154,\r\n      -30\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      153.5,\r\n      -32\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three uniform route longitude offsets (-0.25, 0, +0.25 degrees), crossed with independent start and end latitude offsets (-0.5, 0, +0.5 degrees): 27 finite editorial scenarios. Offsets are OSW choices, not source-reported uncertainty. Intermediate latitude gates stay fixed. Does not span all possible meanders or branch choices. A preliminary -0.5 degree westward route crossed the coarse atlas land mask near 28 degrees S; it was rejected rather than included as a plausible route.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Inspect correspondence with a sourced shelf-break/bathymetric corridor, beyond the coarse atlas land mask.\",\r\n    \"Review northern origin and separation conventions against alternative geographic accounts.\",\r\n    \"Independent physical-oceanography review of the nominal route and scenario choices.\",\r\n    \"Integrate separately scoped candidate geometry and measurement into canonical release and atlas pages before public admission.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1360,\r\n    480,\r\n    160,\r\n    150\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"15°S start\",\r\n    \"32°S usual separation\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Reilly et al. (2026), §1\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"coherent-jet reference route\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"source_retrieval_note\": \"Source passage rechecked 2026-10-03 for protocol migration; original retrieval date was not recorded. Geometry and length unchanged.\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"e057b2d05108b535677b60d33cd4499288daead8468cc620bc7a6fbfee3b3392\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 2110.298,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 2100,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2011.115,\r\n    2212.394\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2000,\r\n    2300\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.5,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.5,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          147.25,\r\n          -15.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          149.25,\r\n          -18\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          152.25,\r\n          -21\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          153.75,\r\n          -24\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          153.75,\r\n          -27\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          153.75,\r\n          -30\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n    