res interface region to a selected 35 N Canary feed-region gate. Excludes Portugal Coastal Current, Portugal Coastal Countercurrent, slope undercurrents, Azores eastward jet and downstream Canary route. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Near-surface offshore southward-flow naming context; 2002 drifters had drogues at 15 m. No depth-specific core or full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from an undated repository chapter, 1993-1994 observations published in 2002, and a 2026 regional synthesis. Selected route is not a dated trajectory or annual/seasonal mean axis.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers12-12/010038152.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Chapter 23 section 2.1, printed p. 880 / PDF page 4: offshore southward Portugal Current from 45-50 N and 10-20 W; coastal circulation described separately.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Aristegui et al., Oceanography and fisheries of the Canary current/Iberian region of the eastern North Atlantic, The Sea volume 14, chapter 23. Repository PDF front matter carries copyright 2004; edition publication year not established here.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2000JC000345\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Martins, Hamann and Fiuza (2002), Surface circulation in the eastern North Atlantic, from drifters and altimetry, JGR Oceans 107(C12), doi:10.1029/2000JC000345.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Sections 2.1 and 3.3.1, Table 2: offshore current distinct from coastal flows; 36-44 N / 24-12 W statistical box.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Identity and sampled-region context; box bounds are not whole-current endpoints or width.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/2059/2026/\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Ibrahim and Sun (2026), A multidecadal sea level rise and its hiatus in the tropical Atlantic margin off northwest Africa, Ocean Science 22, 2059-2081.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 4: combined Portugal/Portugal Coastal system feeds converge with Azores around 35 N.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Southern regional convergence context; does not uniquely locate the offshore-current endpoint.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Every vertex is OSW-selected. The northern source-region range gives three bookkeeping gates at 45, 47.5 and 50 N; nominal gate 47.5 N is a convention, not an inferred midpoint axis. Southern 35 N uses combined-system convergence context. Longitudes and bends are editorial, not digitized observations.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -15,\r\n      47.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15.5,\r\n      45\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15.8,\r\n      43\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15.5,\r\n      41\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15,\r\n      39\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -14.5,\r\n      37\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -13.5,\r\n      35\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_northern_interface_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -15.5,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15.8,\r\n          43\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15.5,\r\n          41\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15,\r\n          39\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -14.5,\r\n          37\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -13.5,\r\n          35\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"45 N northern-interface convention; not observed seasonal contraction.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_interface_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -14.5,\r\n          50\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15,\r\n          47.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15.5,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15.8,\r\n          43\r\n        ]