y_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_B_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_B_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_B_3\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/guiana-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/guiana-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n"},"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_sha256":"64c8f36d57216f978f94ed81debd6f4d8d95b74c985ee613870c3a41d2c7942d","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Subsurface thermocline context of the 2010 model proposal. Its indexed mean-flow discussion uses sigma 24.0-26.5, not a fixed 100-400 m slab. The later 2012 ADCP averages and tracer profiles do not supply one common continuous SICU core layer.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Static OSW geographic reference. The 2010 model mean and July-August 2012 regional observations are separate evidence contexts. Neither dates these editorial vertices or establishes seasonal route changes.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Melet et al. (2010) coauthor abstract proposes SICU east of Solomon Islands; original model axis not acquired. Ganachaud et al. (2017), Figures 2 and 7 and pages 11-12/17, supply island geography and local observational context, not a continuous SICU axis.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Melet, Gourdeau, Kessler, Verron and Molines (2010), Thermocline circulation in the Solomon Sea: A modeling study, J. Phys. Oceanogr. 40, 1302–1319, doi:10.1175/2009JPO4264.1.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Coauthor abstract paraphrased. Ganachaud et al. (2017) original CC BY 4.0 paper retained with attribution; no original scientific figure is incorporated into this editorial map.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-09\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore vertices on the Pacific side of the Solomon Islands. No source figure is digitized and no station 13-to-43 similarity proves a continuous path. Initial central-chain vertices and the farther-offshore variant touched coarse land near Malaita; central vertices were moved east of the island-chain mask and all 81 scenarios regenerated. The drawn reach is a geographic reference with unresolved coastal clearance and core position, not a measured coastal axis.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      162,\r\n      -9.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      161.5,\r\n      -8.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      160.3,\r\n      -7.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      158.6,\r\n      -6.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      157,\r\n      -5.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      155.8,\r\n      -4.6\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"closer_island_sequence\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          161.9,\r\n          -9.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          161.4,\r\n          -8.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          160.2,\r\n          -7.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          158.5,\r\n          -6.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          156.9,\r\n          -5.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          155.7,\r\n          -4.6\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW geographic alternative, not a measured axis or current edge.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"farther_offshore_sequence\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          162.1,\r\n          -9.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          161.6,\r\n          -8.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          160.4,\r\n          -7.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          158.7,\r\n          -6.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          157.1,\r\n          -5.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          155.9,\r\n          -4.6\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW geographic alternative, not a measured axis or current edge.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.1,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.1\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three geographic shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.05/0/+0.05 degree and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.1/0/+0.1 degree: 81 editorial scenarios. Not width, seasonal extent or statistical confidence.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Acquire and visually review the original 2010 model Figure 4 before digitizing a model axis.\",\r\n    \"Review finer coastline and bathymetry, source velocity fields and the density-dependent flow before identifying an actual current core.\",\r\n    \"Resolve complete entrance/exit gates and connectivity to NICU separately; no connector across Solomon Strait is drawn.\",\r\n    \"No whole-current width, annual range, dated footprint or NASA surface identification inferred.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1430,\r\n    453,\r\n    45,\r\n    53\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 0.8,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 1.3,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.25,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Southern offshore gate\",\r\n    \"Northern offshore gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Melet (2010) abstract; Ganachaud (2017) pp11-17\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern Solomon Islands reference reach\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"label\": \"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1525/elementa.221\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Figures 2 and 7; pages 5-7, 11-12 and 17\",\r\n      \"access\": \"Original NOAA-hosted PDF acquired and institutional SHA256 matched; CC BY 4.0 printed page 27; selected pages and figures inspected.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"source_review_receipt\": {\r\n    \"audit_file\": \"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-proposal-scope-audit.json\",\r\n    \"audit_sha256\": \"476ab173d565d7741cadf354abb3ef981b20c3b3c9c2f9d27d80f5d0ea408586\",\r\n    \"source_document_file\": \"research/source-data/ganachaud-solomon-2017/journal-article.pdf\",\r\n    \"source_document_sha256\": \"981f64dfa09125766a185228391a4e8099f98285cedaaaedecccc9533fa03b9e\",\r\n    \"acquisition_file\": \"research/source-data/ganachaud-solomon-2017/acquisition.json\",\r\n    \"acquisition_sha256\": \"938ba5c93669ea72a390046bd9bc00e922605b1c7e17ab0212c18428855677d1\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"d75e61291df10f438ddc2f2201bc272b56593b344baab03d521a91cc914f0b5b\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 900.116,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 900,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    882.674,\r\n    918.081\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    800,\r\n    1000\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.05,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.1,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.1,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          161.95,\r\n          -9.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          161.45,\r\n          -8.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          160.25,\r\n          -7.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          158.54999999999998,\r\n          -6.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          156.95,\r\n          -5.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          155.75,\r\n          -4.699999999999999\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"length_km\": 902.461,\r