irculation, deep dense-water pathways and downstream Ionian continuation.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Near-surface coastal corridor. No bottom/slope dense-water branch or fixed-depth velocity core reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional surface naming convention informed by 1990-2007 drifter context and 2018 regional synthesis. Not a simultaneous drifter trajectory, annual mean axis or route valid during every wind reversal.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/9/713/2013/os-9-713-2013.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Poulain and Hariri (2013), section 3, printed p. 716: southeastward Italian-coast WAC exits western Otranto. Sections 2.1-2.2 and figure 1: 1990-2007 near-surface drifters and distinct outflow section; 40 N is a basin residence-time boundary, not a current endpoint.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Poulain and Hariri (2013), Transit and residence times in the Adriatic Sea surface as derived from drifter data and Lagrangian numerical simulations, Ocean Science 9, 713-720, doi:10.5194/os-9-713-2013.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Sciascia et al. (2018), Linking sardine recruitment in coastal areas to ocean currents using surface drifters and HF radar: a case study in the Gulf of Manfredonia, Adriatic Sea, doi:10.5194/os-14-1461-2018.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 2.1: buoyant Po-forced WAC along Italian coast and wind modulation; section 2.2: separate Gulf of Manfredonia setting.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Surface branch identity and regional origin; local HF radar/larval paths do not define the full current axis.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects every offshore vertex, the Po-region start and western Otranto terminal gates at 40.4 N and 40.0 N. These are regional bookkeeping gates, not observed named-flow termination bounds. Source outflow-section coordinates in a rotated local frame are not silently reinterpreted as longitude/latitude; no drifter tracks or mean vectors digitized. Offsets test only selected editorial geography.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      13,\r\n      45\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      12.9,\r\n      44.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      13.2,\r\n      44.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      13.8,\r\n      43.65\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      14,\r\n      43.4\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      14.6,\r\n      42.7\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      15.2,\r\n      42.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      16.1,\r\n      42.15\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      16.6,\r\n      41.85\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      16.65,\r\n      41.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      17,\r\n      41.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      17.6,\r\n      40.9\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      18.3,\r\n      40.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      18.6,\r\n      40.4\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_otranto_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          13,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          12.9,\r\n          44.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.2,\r\n          44.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.8,\r\n          43.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          14,\r\n          43.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          14.6,\r\n          42.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          15.2,\r\n          42.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          16.1,\r\n          42.15\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          16.6,\r\n          41.85\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          16.65,\r\n          41.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          17,\r\n          41.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          17.6,\r\n          40.9\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.3,\r\n          40.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.6,\r\n          40.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.75,\r\n          40.0\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative OSW southern Otranto approach gate; 40 N source basin boundary does not prove current termination.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Two regional Otranto gate choices crossed with longitude and independent endpoint latitude offsets of -0.05/0/+0.05 degrees: 54 editorial scenarios, not empirical endpoint uncertainty.\",\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    840,\r\n    250,\r\n    65,\r\n    65\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Po-region approach\",\r\n    \"Western Otranto gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Poulain & Hariri (2013); Sciascia (2018)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Italian-coast surface corridor\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"63652dc63bf24dbb7853b4abc7b28f82a835eef1dc7a8d1f78e7feeea3371340\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 738.654,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 700,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    729.826,\r\n    795.709\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    700,\r\n    800\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.05,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.05,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.05,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          12.95,\r\n          44.95\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          12.85,\r\n          44.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.149999999999999,\r\n          44.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.75,\r\n          43.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.95,\r\n        