\"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_C_2\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/balearic-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/balearic-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n"},"research/jutland-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_sha256":"3a68dca59468fe3ca9ad06e3d1a6fca356775bb6624b0bfc173c7da1a7c1992b","source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Source regional geography paraphrased with attribution; no source figures, curves or velocity data packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 0.85,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 1.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.32,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Scientific review of named-flow gates and regional scope.\",\r\n    \"Verify shelf/slope correspondence with reproducible bathymetry or suitable velocity data.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; these are editorial route lengths.\",\r\n    \"Resolve North/South Jutland labels and validate offshore gates before any branch taxonomy or canonical length admission.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"jutland\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Jutland Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Danish west-coast reference corridor from an OSW German Bight approach gate to an offshore northern-Jutland/Skagerrak approach gate. Excludes upstream English Channel and southern North Sea circuits, Baltic Current inflow and Norwegian Coastal Current continuation. No North/South Jutland branch lengths or aliases admitted.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Regional near-surface coastal naming context; not Atlantic bottom-water inflows or a reconstructed depth-specific core.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"General regional circulation descriptions in 2015 and 2024 research papers. Not a contemporaneous trajectory, annual mean axis or seasonal route series; source sea-level seasonality is not a current-length measurement.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2024.1416519/full\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1.3: Jutland Current transports material north along Danish coast into Skagerrak; subsequent Baltic/Norwegian coastal circulation is distinct. Figure 1 caption labels North and South Jutland currents separately; neither is silently merged as an alias here.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Lenz et al. (2024), Provenance of clay-sized detrital sediments in the North Sea and the Skagerrak region based on radiogenic Nd-Sr-Hf isotopes and clay mineral compositions: assessing the impact of coastal and seabed erosion, Frontiers in Marine Science 11, doi:10.3389/fmars.2024.1416519.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2014JC010510\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Passaro et al. (2015), Annual sea level variability of the coastal ocean: The Baltic Sea-North Sea transition zone, doi:10.1002/2014JC010510.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 2, Area of Study, first paragraph: surface Jutland flow carries Atlantic/German Bight water and turns into the Norwegian Coastal Current after encountering Baltic water.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Surface-flow and naming-transition context; sea-level annual cycle does not supply current geometry or width.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects every offshore vertex and the bookkeeping gates at 54.8 N and northern Jutland. The source names regions and circulation but does not publish these vertices, an exact origin/termination or a full-current length. An alternative southern approach and Skagerrak gate tests endpoint convention. No source figure arrows, sediment trajectories or velocity fields digitized; offsets are editorial sensitivity only.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      7.45,\r\n      54.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      7.5,\r\n      55.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      7.7,\r\n      55.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      7.85,\r\n      56.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      8.05,\r\n      56.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      8.45,\r\n      57.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      9.2,\r\n      57.65\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      10.3,\r\n      57.88\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_approach_extended_skagerrak_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          7.2,\r\n          54.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          7.5,\r\n          55.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          7.7,\r\n          55.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          7.85,\r\n          56.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          8.05,\r\n          56.8\r\n        ],\r\