g the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/north-cape-northern-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/north-cape-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n"},"research/persian-gulf-cascading-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_sha256":"701cab9d83dde9a05cc9b2f18418b73667b1cad70e8230e1d39449f55e4451cb","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"persian-gulf-saline-overflow\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Persian Gulf saline overflow\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Northern outflow/cascading reference reach: OSW upstream truncation near 26 N, then the source-described vicinity of 25deg20N,57E and 24deg50N,56deg50E. No Arabian Sea downstream route or whole-system origin/termination.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Descending Persian Gulf Water core; near 220 m neutral-buoyancy description is downstream context, not a fixed 220 m trajectory or surface-current route.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"October-November1999 GOGP99 study geography. Editorial line joins regional descriptions; not one synoptic snapshot, monthly geometry or an R13 width occupation.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00000/390/83.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Part2 author version abstract PDF1 and regional pathways discussion printed pp4-6/PDF5-7. Source supplies approximate cascade/rejoining geography, not a digitized axis.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Pous, S.P., Carton, X. and Lazure, P. (2004), Hydrology and circulation in the Strait of Hormuz and the Gulf of Oman: Results from the GOGP99 Experiment, parts 1 and 2, JGR Oceans 109, doi:10.1029/2003JC002145 and doi:10.1029/2003JC002146. Institutional author versions.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Copyright 2004 AGU; no open redistribution license assigned. Original author versions ignored; attributed geography and independent OSW sketch only.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-09\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects offshore regional gates and rounded vertices within the described geography. Alternative shapes shift intermediate latitudes by +/- 0.2 degree; longitude and independent endpoint-latitude shifts test drawing convention. These choices are not measured current boundaries, physical uncertainty or seasonal extrema.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      56.65,\r\n      26\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      56.9,\r\n      25.65\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      57,\r\n      25.333333333333332\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      56.833333333333336,\r\n      24.833333333333332\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"eastward_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          56.65,\r\n          26\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.333333333333332\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.833333333333336,\r\n          24.833333333333332\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial offshore bend; not a second occupation or measured current axis.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"straighter_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          56.65,\r\n          26\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.85,\r\n          25.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.333333333333332\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.833333333333336,\r\n          24.833333333333332\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative interpolation among source-described regions; not physical uncertainty.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.03,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.03\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared shapes crossed with three uniform longitude shifts and independent three-value endpoint latitude shifts: 81 retained editorial scenarios, not confidence limits or seasonal ranges.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 10,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Independently review identity, layer, selected gates and fine coastline/bathymetry before physical admission.\",\r\n    \"Acquire dated velocity or suitable physical geometry before measuring a current axis or meander length.\",\r\n    \"Whole-current length, physical width and annual ranges remain unresolved.\",\r\n    \"No seasonal playback, occupied polygon, physical state containment or NASA current identity inferred.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1019,\r\n    337,\r\n    35,\r\n    39\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 0.55,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 0.9,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.25,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"OSW upstream truncation\",\r\n    \"Source-described slope vicinity\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Pous et al. (2004), part2 abstract\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Northern outflow/cascading reference reach\",\r\n  \"source_review_receipt\": {\r\n    \"source_document_file\": \"research/source-data/pous-oman-2004/journal-article.pdf\",\r\n    \"source_document_sha256\": \"3666cd028afd96bd4e1ca33bca27e6de43ed3cd4b17c4eeb40f48f672aeeaaf7\",\r\n    \"acquisition_file\": \"research/source-data/pous-oman-2004/acquisition.json\",\r\n    \"acquisition_sha256\": \"b126b6b250168361fb7bfe572a4028150fe17f0f41f6e49ebc9cbafe0c68791f\",\r\n    \"audit_file\": \"research/persian-gulf-cascading-reach-scope-audit.json\",\r\n    \"audit_sha256\": \"28a1de3affa2d420a4aef6a26d9030eb0a1e6c60bd1d4