 toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Descending dense Red Sea outflow plume branch, with bottom and interfacial layers and changing equilibrium depth. Not a surface flow, fixed 100-250 m depth slab, channel width or equilibrated-water boundary undercurrent.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"REDSOX winter/summer 2001 geographic branch context; selected path is editorial, not a synoptic velocity axis or reconstructed seasonal routes. Cruises and station composites are separate occupations.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Peters et al. (2005), section 2, section 3a and Figure 1 printed571 / PDF3 identify two preferred descending plume pathways. Section5a printed575 / PDF7 describes non-synoptic velocity-supported northern reach 130 km; channel lengths / 5 km width are different objects. Source figure inspected for orientation only.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Peters, Johns, Bower and Fratantoni (2005), Mixing and Entrainment in the Red Sea Outflow Plume. Part I: Plume Structure, Journal of Physical Oceanography 35, 569-583.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Copyright 2005 American Meteorological Society. Original retained locally and ignored; independently selected OSW vertices and attributed facts only. No source figure or bathymetric curve copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-13\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Source supports the declared regional geography or study-domain convention. OSW selects all gates, rounded connecting vertices and alternative bends; no velocity axis or source trajectory reconstructed. Independent longitude and endpoint-latitude shifts describe drawing choices, not current width, source position errors or seasonal extrema.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      43.3,\r\n      12.7\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.45,\r\n      12.52\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.52,\r\n      12.38\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.61,\r\n      12.24\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.67,\r\n      12.12\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          43.3,\r\n          12.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.45,\r\n          12.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.52,\r\n          12.360000000000001\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.61,\r\n          12.22\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.67,\r\n          12.12\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the declared regional gates; not a measured seasonal state.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          43.3,\r\n          12.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.45,\r\n          12.54\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.52,\r\n          12.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.61,\r\n          12.26\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.67,\r\n          12.12\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the declared regional gates; not a measured seasonal state.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.01,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.01\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.02,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.02\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared shapes with three longitude shifts and independent three-value endpoint latitude shifts: 81 retained editorial scenarios, not statistical uncertainty or annual variation.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 10,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_ro