range_interpretation\": \"Approximate meridional span from descriptive source latitude limits. No numerical error bars, annual extrema or full-width inference.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"90 E local section: described band 1.2 S to 1.5 N. Not the full 2 S to 2 N survey or a longitudinal route.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Meridional latitude span; not a diagnosed flow-normal width.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Author-described strong saline eastward band within the 80–150 m depth range. Not a fixed-depth slice or the width at every depth.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"1–3 March 2017 Indonesia PRIMA campaign section. A dated local sample, not recurring March geometry.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Described co-occurrence of strong eastward flow and saline water. No numerical lateral velocity threshold or paired velocity edges established; salinity transport contours remain distinct.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055/noaa_64055_DS1.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Siswanto, Kusmanto and McPhaden (2019), Estimated transport of Equatorial Undercurrent observed at 90 E during the Indonesia Prima 2017 campaign, IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science 303, 012005, doi:10.1088/1755-1315/303/1/012005.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Data and Methods, printed p. 3 / PDF index 3, sampling dates; Results p. 4 and Conclusions p. 5 / indices 4–5, reported latitude/depth band.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_dated_SADCP_CTD_band_description\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Reported latitude limits transcribed from text and converted with WGS84 meridional distance; rounded to 10 km. No source figure or velocity edges digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independent extraction review and canonical admission.\",\r\n        \"Diagnose flow-normal velocity boundaries and repeated compatible sections before current widths or annual ranges.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"1–3 March 2017 subsurface band\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"dated_band_section\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": {\r\n        \"start\": \"2017-03-01\",\r\n        \"end\": \"2017-03-03\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"time_precision\": \"day\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"subsurface_band_context\": {\r\n        \"source_reported_latitude_limits_degrees\": [\r\n          -1.2,\r\n          1.5\r\n        ],\r\n        \"section_longitude_degrees_east\": 90,\r\n        \"source_reported_depth_range_m\": [\r\n          80,\r\n          150\r\n        ],\r\n        \"method\": \"WGS84_meridional_distance_between_reported_latitude_limits\",\r\n        \"unrounded_distance_km\": 298.5511199778176,\r\n        \"rounding_km\": 10,\r\n        \"span_is_width_at_every_depth\": false,\r\n        \"paired_velocity_edges_diagnosed\": false,\r\n        \"depth_range_is_uniform_axis_layer\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_boundary_m_s\": null\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"indian-seuc-bran-mam-core-spatial-summary\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_climatological_threshold_core_distribution\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"maximum_meridional_extent_of_3d_threshold_core\",\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"median of meridional threshold-core extents across longitudes\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 169,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": [\r\n        26,\r\n        294\r\n      ],\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"spatial_range_of_climatological_threshold_core_spans\",\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Across-longitude min/max of March-May climatological core extents; not seasonal extrema, measurement uncertainty or a confidence interval.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Source Indian SEUC longitude sections; not a uniform width along the OSW reach.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Meridional extent at each longitude, not a reconstructed flow-normal span.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Three-dimensional u>0.1 m/s core; maximum meridional extent across depth. Separate from the representative isopycnal route context.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"March-May BRAN2020 monthly climatology using 2001-2018. Width of a climatological field; not an average of instantaneous widths.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Strict eastward zonal u>0.1 m/s core; author defines maximum meridional extent at each longitude.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Chen, Han, Zu, Chu and Chen (2022), The Deep-Penetrating South Equatorial Undercurrent in the Tropical South Indian Ocean, Geophysical Research Letters 49, e2022GL098163, doi:10.1029/2022GL098163.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 2 data averaging; Section 3 core definition and width paragraph; Figure 3 caption.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_model_climatological_core_analysis\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Author-reported median and spatial range transcribed; no contours or velocity arrays digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independently reproduce the 3D threshold-core extent and longitude aggregation from BRAN.\",\r\n        \"Recover matching monthly sections before seasonal width changes or annual extrema.\",\r\n        \"Canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"March-May climatological core\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"climatological_core_distribution\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"maximum_meridional_extent_of_3d_core\",\r\n      \"core_distribution_context\": {\r\n        \"product\": \"BRAN2020\",\r\n        \"averaging_period_years\": [\r\n          2001,\r\n          2018\r\n        ],\r\n        \"climatology_months\": [\r\n          3,\r\n          4,\r\n          5\r\n        ],\r\n        \"velocity_component\": \"zonal_u\",\r\n        \"velocity_threshold_m_s\": 0.1,\r\n        \"threshold_operator\": \">\",\r\n        \"core_extent_statistic\": \"maximum_meridional_extent_across_depth_at_each_longitude\",\r\n        \"summary_statistic\": \"median_across_longitudes\",\r\n        \"range_axis\": \"longitude\",\r\n        \"averaging_before_boundary_detection\": true,\r\n        \"is_mean_of_instantaneous_widths\": false,\r\n        \"full_width_at_each_depth\": false\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"mauritanian-upwelling-seasonal-mean-width-range\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"mauritanian\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Mauritanian Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_seasonal_mean_width_range\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": [\r\n        30,\r\n        40\r\n      ],\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"author_reported_width_span_of_seasonal_mean_section\",\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Approximate author-reported span for the upwelling-season mean undercurrent section. Not annual extrema, confidence limits or a mean of instantaneous widths; no midpoint selected.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Reference section at 18 N, pooling coastal measurements from 17–19 N by local bathymetry. Not a uniform whole-coast width.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Across-shore reference section; rotated alongshore velocity and topographic remapping, not extracted paired edge coordinates.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Poleward subsurface flow with core context about 100–200 m in the seasonal mean. No fixed-depth boundary pair assigned; equatorward shelf surface flow and deeper return remain separate.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"December–April upwelling-season convention; five cruises sampled in January–April during 2005–2011 within the study-wide 2005–2016 campaign set. December label is not evidence for sampled December geometry.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author reports 30–40 km in Conclusion; numerical velocity threshold and paired boundaries for this prose width were not extracted.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014264\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Klenz, Dengler and Brandt (2018), Seasonal Variability of the Mauritania Current and Hydrography at 18 N, JGR: Oceans 123, 8122–8137, doi:10.1029/2018JC014264.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 5 width statement; section 2.1 and Table 2 sampling/remapping; section 3.1 and Figure 5 seasonal mean context.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_publication_year\": 2018,\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_observational_seasonal_mean_summary\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Width span transcribed from publisher conclusion; figures, edges and source arrays not digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Recover paired boundaries and thresholds for the source seasonal mean.\",\r\n        \"Obtain compatible relaxation/other-season repeat widths; no annual extrema yet.\",\r\n        \"Independent canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"December–April poleward undercurrent · seasonal mean\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_mean_width_range\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2,\r\n        3,\r\n        4\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Five upwelling cruises support this mean. August 2016 was excluded from both seasonal means. The 60 km transport window and 200 km surface-flow context are not current widths.\",\r\n      \"calendar_source_locator\": \"Section 2.1 seasonal cruise assignment and Figure 5 caption.\",\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_mean_context\": {\r\n        \"reference_latitude_degrees\": 18,\r\n        \"pooled_latitude_bounds_degrees\": [\r\n          17,\r\n          19\r\n        ],\r\n        \"sample_years\": [\r\n          2005,\r\n          2011\r\n        ],\r\n        \"study_years\": [\r\n          2005,\r\n          2016\r\n        ],\r\n        \"cruise_ids\": [\r\n          \"P320\",\r\n          \"P347\",\r\n          \"P348\",\r\n          \"ATA3\",\r\n          \"MSM17/4\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"sampled_months\": [\r\n          1,\r\n          2,\r\n          3,\r\n          4\r\n        ],\r\n        \"averaging_rule\": \"Measurements rotated locally, sorted by water depth, remapped onto reference topography, then assigned to source seasonal means.\",\r\n        \"width_of_mean_section\": true,\r\n        \"mean_of_instantaneous_widths\": false,\r\n        \"paired_edges_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"fixed_depth_bounds_m\": null\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-secc-1994-03-described-band-span\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_month_section_angular_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_meridional_angular_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 220,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Converted local band span only. No uncertainty interval, uniform along-route width, annual range or continuous current axis inferred.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"March 1994 CITHER 2 section at 30 W, reported current band 6–8 S; local meridional span, not whole-current extent.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Reported meridional section span; no exact flow-normal reinterpretation or observed paired-edge geometry.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Two eastward-core contexts near 40 m and 240 m, separated by westward flow near 110 m. Reported band extends to at least 400 m in the section; its span is not a width at every depth.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"March 1994 section label; precise local occupation days unextracted. Cruise-wide dates are not assigned to this section.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Section 4.1 describes flow within 6–8 S. Paired velocity edges at a chosen depth and a reproducible threshold remain unextracted.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Bourles, Gouriou and Chuchla (1999), On the circulation in the upper layer of the western equatorial Atlantic, JGR Oceans 104(C9), 21151–21170, doi:10.1029/1999JC900058.\",\r\n      \"