tion; no specific width section or endpoints supplied.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Unspecified in institutional prose; no occupied section extracted.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Source describes a typical 200 m depth extent; this does not specify a fixed depth or vertically averaged layer for the 30 km width.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Undated typical description in a plan dated 25 September 2014 for 2015-25. These are document dates, not width observation dates or a seasonal cycle.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Typical current-width description without paired edges, a speed threshold or a specified occupied section.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://imos.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/NSW-IMOS_Node_Plan_2015-25_Final.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Robertson, Ingleton, Doblin, Suthers and Roughan, NSW-IMOS Node Science and Implementation Plan 2015-25, edited Robin Robertson, dated 25 September 2014, section 3.3.1.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.3.1, printed page 23 (PDF page index 22), first paragraph; plan date on printed page 2: 25 September 2014.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-04\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"institutional_science_plan_prose_synthesis\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate scalar transcribed from institutional PDF text; no figure, influence envelope, array span or route buffer measured.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Typical current width in NSW-IMOS plan\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_scalar_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"regional_scalar_context\": {\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/east-australian-imos-regional-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"c051be2ee7863179fc447a22a9055f7ff501ed8dcc0ed5f104f390d3343e4b40\",\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_supplied\": false,\r\n        \"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer\": false,\r\n        \"reported_depth_extent_is_fixed_measurement_layer\": false\r\n      },\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Inspect Mata et al. (2000) and Ridgway and Dunn (2003) for the width convention and support.\",\r\n        \"Recover compatible layer-specific cross-flow sections and observations through seasons.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific claim admission.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Underlying width convention remains unverified. CSIRO describes a separate 100 km strong-influence width, which is not combined with the 30 km typical current summary into a seasonal range. The 240 km mooring array and 200 km eddy diameters are different quantities. Institutional PDF text was inspected; screenshot acquisition failed.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"leeuwin-a101-monthly-fit-04\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"leeuwin\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Leeuwin Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_monthly_mean_fitted_width\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"source_fitted_cross_flow_width\",\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"a101; mean of source fitted widths\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 132,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Two extracted monthly climatological values do not establish a full annual range or a confidence interval.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"TOPEX/Poseidon ascending track a101 crossing near 26 S, west of Western Australia. No monthly lateral-edge coordinates extracted.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-flow width corrected from oblique satellite track using theta=43.45 degrees.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface geostrophic diagnostic from absolute SSH minus AUSGeoid98. The 80 m layer is a transport assumption, not the width measurement layer.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Calendar-month composite of per-cycle fitted widths. Section 3.3 says January 1993-July 2002; Fig. 7 caption says through August 2002. Exact combined period unresolved; no single-year occupation inferred.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Source w=1.89*L*cos(theta), described as about 50% of maximum fitted velocity; preserve approximate source coefficient rather than exact half-maximum conversion.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/21be/8b2802335b0f945b23cde6ece4d5e3647f09.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Deng, Hwang, Coleman and Featherstone (2008), Seasonal and Interannual Variations of the Leeuwin Current off Western Australia from TOPEX/Poseidon Satellite Altimetry, TAO 19, 135-149, doi:10.3319/TAO.2008.19.1-2.135(SA).\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.3, printed page 143, paragraph discussing current width at a101; Fig. 7d on page 144; section 2.2 equations 1-3 on page 138 and angle convention on page 139.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-04\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_altimetry_fitted_monthly_width\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate April/September values transcribed from source prose and visually checked against Fig. 7d; no other monthly points inferred.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"April climatological fitted width\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"monthly_climatological_fit\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": 