l methods.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Study velocity-field context September 1999-August 2000. No exact width occupations, seasonal width series or annual extrema extracted.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Approximate regional current width reported in the abstract; paired edges and a width-defining velocity cutoff are not supplied there. Reported 0.2-0.4 m/s flow is velocity context, not an edge threshold.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10872-006-0004-3\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Ohshima, K. I., Wakatsuchi, M. and Saitoh, S. I. (2005), Velocity Field of the Oyashio Region Observed with Satellite-Tracked Surface Drifters during 1999-2000, Journal of Oceanography 61, 845-855, doi:10.1007/s10872-006-0004-3.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Publisher abstract, regional current-width sentence.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_publisher_abstract\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed publisher abstract numerical description; full original methods and figures not inspected.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Publisher abstract regional description\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_scalar_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Inspect full original methods and figures to recover the width convention, layer and spatial support.\",\r\n        \"Obtain compatible dated repeat sections before seasonal animation or annual ranges.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific and canonical admission review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Source access: publisher abstract inspected (California via publisher-indexed text). Full original methods, figures and boundary definitions remain unreviewed; no original PDF acquisition claimed.\",\r\n      \"source_scope_context\": {\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_supplied\": false,\r\n        \"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer\": false,\r\n        \"dataset_period_is_width_sampling_period\": false,\r\n        \"full_original_inspected\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_context_is_boundary_cutoff\": false,\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/oyashio-2005-abstract-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"7fd3b4cfbe3249d7d7e4ea78242d3f809db99e6a9d2b6f8c2a7d5ea42693c605\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"regional_scalar_context\": {\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_supplied\": false,\r\n        \"bathymetry_is_measurement_layer\": false,\r\n        \"dataset_period_is_width_sampling_period\": false,\r\n        \"full_original_inspected\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_context_is_boundary_cutoff\": false,\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/oyashio-2005-abstract-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"7fd3b4cfbe3249d7d7e4ea78242d3f809db99e6a9d2b6f8c2a7d5ea42693c605\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"somali-schott-2001-march-may-coastal-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_seasonal_regional_prose_width_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_seasonal_regional_current_scale\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": [\r\n        50,\r\n        100\r\n      ],\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"One seasonal regional prose span, not an annual range, probability interval or three monthly measurements. Other months have no compatible width evidence here.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Northern Somali coastal upwelling regime, farther north than the southern EACC extension that turns offshore near 3-4 N. Northern latitude limits unresolved; no width assigned to the southern gyre, Great Whirl or the entire Somali Current.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"No reproducible section endpoints extracted from the original review prose.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Shallow northward coastal flow overlying a southward undercurrent; no numerical fixed layer or velocity threshold extracted for the width.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"March-May seasonal synthesis in the 2001 review; no specific year, exact occupied section dates or monthly width values supplied.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-reported order-of-magnitude width scale of the northern shallow coastal flow. Paired geographic edges and a speed cutoff are unextracted.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Schott, F. A. and McCreary, J. P. Jr. (2001), The monsoon circulation of the Indian Ocean, Progress in Oceanography 51, 1-123, doi:10.1016/S0079-6611(01)00083-0.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4.1.1, printed p. 38 (PDF page 38), March-May paragraph, final sentence and preceding northern-flow context.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_seasonal_synthesis_of_prior_observations\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Numerical seasonal width scale transcribed from inspected full original prose; no contour, section or raw observation digitization.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"March-May northern coastal flow\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_regional_width_range\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        3,\r\n        4,\r\n        5\r\n      ],\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Recover underlying dated northern coastal sections and boundary convention.\",\r\n        \"Obtain compatible repeat widths across the other nine months before a yearly cycle.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific and canonical admission.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Full original review inspected and printed p. 38 rendered. This is a seasonal synthesis; underlying width occupations and boundary methods remain unextracted.\",\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"author_reported_seasonal_regional_width_scale_span\",\r\n      \"calendar_source_locator\": \"Section 4.1.1, printed p. 38 (PDF page 38), March-May paragraph heading.\",\r\n      \"seasonal_regional_context\": {\r\n        \"southern_turnoff_latitude_is_width_edge\": false,\r\n        \"undercurrent_is_same_width_layer\": false,\r\n        \"Great_Whirl_scale_is_coastal_width\": false,\r\n        \"season_months_are_monthly_measurements\": false,\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"full_original_inspected\": true,\r\n        \"protocol_file\": \"plans/somali-seasonal-width-protocol-v1.md\",\r\n        \"protocol_sha256\": \"5182a21bd951600e62581469470a0cf3a2b74d2ab17a7475e93d070d7e90e53a\",\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/somali-schott-2001-premonsoon-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"726977308ec5be08932acf561d01d05c350778a9aad78cebb0770ef375cd5388\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"guinea-djakoure-2017-reference-mean-regional-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"guinea\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Guinea Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_model_regional_prose_width\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_regional_width_of_annual_mean_reference_model_surface_flow\",\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"Regional annual-mean reference-model width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 200,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"One approximate regional model-mean width; numerical uncertainty and monthly/annual extrema unresolved. The separate theoretical 210 km inertial scale is not a width bound.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Northern Gulf of Guinea: eastward surface current between 2 N and African coast; no paired geographic edges extracted.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"No paired transverse section endpoints extracted; published regional model comparison prose.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface velocity field; numerical top-cell depth unextracted. Introductory 30-40 m thickness is not assigned as a width layer.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Reference model years 5-10, from a ten-year climatologically forced ROMS integration. Model years are not calendar years; annual mean is not an annual width minimum/maximum.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Approximate width reported in model comparison prose; cutoff and paired section boundaries unextracted.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00391/50248/69638.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Djakoure, S., Penven, P., Bourles, B., Kone, V., and Veitch, J. (2017). Respective Roles of the Guinea Current and Local Winds on the Coastal Upwelling in the Northern Gulf of Guinea. Journal of Physical Oceanography 47, 1367-1387. doi:10.1175/JPO-D-16-0126.1\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"printed p1379, section 3c(2), first paragraph; Figure 1d context in section 3a(1), pp1371-1372\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_reference_model_regional_mean\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate width transcribed from inspected original p1379 prose; no figure, contour or model-field digitization.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Regional annual-mean reference model\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"model_regional_width_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Resolve top-cell depth and model figure caption conflict before edge digitization.\",\r\n        \"Acquire compatible repeated regional boundaries before monthly/annual variation.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific admission.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Original institutionally hosted publisher article inspected. Figure 1 caption calls model panels idealized while section 3a(1) calls them reference; width retained from explicit p1379 reference-experiment prose.\",\r\n      \"model_regional_context\": {\r\n        \"model\": {\r\n          \"parent_resolution_degrees\": 0.2,\r\n          \"child_resolution_degrees\": 0.06666666666666667,\r\n          \"ten_year_climatological_integration\": true,\r\n          \"analysis_model_years\": [\r\n            5,\r\n            6,\r\n            7,\r\n            8,\r\n            9,\r\n            10\r\n          ],\r\n          \"calendar_dates\": null\r\n        },\r\n        \"theoretical_inertial_scale_is_width_bound\": false,\r\n        \"model_years_are_calendar_years\": false,\r\n        \"annual_mean_is_annual_extrema\": false,\r\n        \"introduction_thickness_is_fixed_width_layer\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_maximum_is_boundary_cutoff\": false,\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"figure_caption_conflict_resolved\": false,\r\n        \"full_original_inspected\": true,\r\n        \"protocol_file\": \"plans/guinea-model-regional-width-protocol-v1.md\",\r\n        \"protocol_sha256\": \"10fc2a7ad5855a266e9a7b1d2f21dc74d957f8b7dba968ad3db4472f9cf7df29\",\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/guinea-djakoure-2017-model-width-source-review.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"15d7b34f39d840541cb5d10deb0fac79f029640866ebc0c0acd61dc5dfd5eea6\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"algerian-cotroneo-2019-regional-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"algerian\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Algerian Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": [\r\n        30,\r\n        50\r\n      ],\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"reported_typical_regional_width_span\",\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"One reported regional along-slope width span; not annual extrema, a confidence interval, three autumn observations or a selected midpoint.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Eastward along-slope Atlantic Water flow along the Algerian coast after leaving the Alboran Sea; no exact longitudinal terminal gates or paired width edges supplied.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"No reproducible transverse section endpoints supplied for the introductory width description.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface Atlantic Water regional flow; numerical width layer unresolved. Dataset sampling down to 975 m is not assigned as a width layer.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Regional background synthesis in a 2019 article; no width occupation dates or calendar supplied. Autumn 2014-2016 describes the separate ABACUS survey dataset.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-reported regional span, citing Testor et al. (2005). No paired edge positions or velocity cutoff