th_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"source_reported_composite_point_no_width_error\",\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Approximate width of the historical upper-core float composite. Repeated 100 km subset entries do not establish constant width, annual extrema or numerical width uncertainty.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Tropical western Atlantic upper-core DWBC; Table 2 selection domain 2 S-12 N west of 43 W; section 3.2 labels a 0-7 N / 12-month composite. Source domains retained without forced equivalence.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Distance seaward of 1800 m isobath; velocity rotated parallel and normal to that contour.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Nominal 1800 m SOFAR floats; failed active depth control and source-estimated sinking about 230 m over 21 months. No fixed numerical width layer.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Table 2 historical composite label January 1989-October 1990, overlapping three unequal subsets. No exact width observation dates or recurring seasonal calendar extracted.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Width between zero-velocity points in the composite along-boundary velocity profile, flanked by weak counterflow/recirculation; 10 km averaging bins do not supply a width error.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/93JC00051\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Richardson, P. L. and Schmitz, W. J., Jr. (1993), Deep Cross-Equatorial Flow in the Atlantic Measured With SOFAR Floats, Journal of Geophysical Research 98(C5), 8371-8387, doi:10.1029/93JC00051.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Final original PDF p5 / printed p8375, section 3.2 continuation; Table 2 PDF p8 / p8378; nominal depth and processing p2; subset sampling p6 and Figure 6 p7.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-09\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_original_lagrangian_velocity_composite\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Visually reviewed numerical passage, Table 