are a subset of the 100–200 km western span. Figure 3 variability-envelope widths, 80/340 km SLA smoothing, core displacement and offshore core position remain distinct metrics. No seasonal width animation inferred.\",\r\n        \"quality_note\": \"Complete unchanged HAL deposit inspected. Author regional numbers retained with their metrics and seasonal context; paired boundaries and numeric errors not recovered.\",\r\n        \"source_pdf_sha256\": \"6da50667b80790752fa0189ff9cf0cdfd88c521509b0f393365de306286bacbe\",\r\n        \"protocol_file\": \"plans/ngcc-seasonal-vein-width-protocol-v1.md\",\r\n        \"protocol_sha256\": \"e39b24d49fea763f129e82e9c76dbaa6f2e23b6d5485ffb6e4008ee5b4038d73\",\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"full_width_conversion_admitted\": false,\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/ngcc-radenac-2016-seasonal-vein-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"223405cce3aa4a5fecdf94dd25ebff225a9594f33fb04f784a469fd4e6e8ce10\",\r\n        \"audit_pointer\": \"/measurements/1\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n      \"name\": \"New Guinea Coastal Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_summary\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_summary\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://hal.science/hal-01497605/document#page=13\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Radenac, M.-H., Leger, F., Messie, M., Dutrieux, P., Menkes, C. and Eldin, G. (2016), Wind-driven changes of surface current, temperature, and chlorophyll observed by satellites north of New Guinea, JGR Oceans 121, 2231-2252, doi:10.1002/2015JC011438.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 5.1 and Figure 10, printed p2242 / retained PDF13; seasonal climatology section 5 printed p2240 / PDF11; altimetry methods printed pp2235-2236 / PDF6-7.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-13\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"primary_author_seasonal_surface_vein_descriptor\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Author prose values transcribed from visually reviewed original. No velocity/SST edges digitized and no averaging of regional descriptors.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Author along-track regional surface descriptions; nearly coast-normal satellite tracks, with no flow-normal correction or paired coordinates independently reconstructed.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface altimetric current anomaly or SST-associated surface water-mass vein, depending on metric. No uniform depth slab; 50-100 m upwelling and deeper NGCUC support not transferred.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Trade-wind / austral-winter context. Section 5 describes 2001-2010 reconstructed monthly climatology with 150-500 day seasonal signals; Figure 10 illustrates August and February. These regional widths are winter descriptors illustrated in August, not widths dated for every winter month or individual year.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-described surface vein span. Exact seasonal velocity-anomaly threshold and paired geographic edges not specified in this descriptor. Figure 3 half-maximum anomaly-standard-deviation region is a different operator.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\r\n      \"time_precision\": \"regional_seasonal_description_not_exact_width_dates\",\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Complete unchanged HAL deposit inspected. Author regional numbers retained with their metrics and seasonal context; paired boundaries and numeric errors not recovered.\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Recover compatible surface current and SST boundary criteria before physical comparison.\",\r\n        \"Recover repeated matching sections before annual extrema or seasonal width geometry.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"id\": \"ngcc-radenac-2016-winter-west-maxima\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Western widest sections / tracks 023 and 201\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Two widest western surface current-anomaly locations at tracks 023 and 201. One near-200 km descriptor applies to both; not an average or independent pair.\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 200,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_seasonal_surface_current_anomaly_vein_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"surface current-anomaly vein span\",\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"seasonal_regional_point_descriptor_not_temporal_range\",\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Author approximate regional point descriptor; numeric uncertainty and annual variation unknown.\",\r\n      \"original_regional_context\": {\r\n        \"description_kind\": \"ngcc_trade_wind_current_anomaly_vein\",\r\n        \"source_claim_id\": \"radenac2016-5.1-current-anomaly-vein-widths\",\r\n        \"descriptors_are_independent_replicates\": false,\r\n        \"reported_tracks\": [\r\n          \"023\",\r\n          \"201\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"source_season\": \"austral winter / southeast trade winds\",\r\n        \"source_illustrated_month\": 8,\r\n        \"source_section_climatology_years\": [\r\n          2001,\r\n          2010\r\n        ],\r\n        \"source_section_seasonal_filter_days\": [\r\n          150,\r\n          500\r\n        ],\r\n        \"source_native_along_track_spacing_km\": 6.1,\r\n        \"source_f_plane_sla_filter_fwhm_km\": 80,\r\n        \"source_beta_plane_sla_filter_fwhm_km\": 340,\r\n        \"preprocessing_scales_are_current_widths\": false,\r\n        \"figure3_variability_envelope_transferred\": false,\r\n        \"paired_velocity_boundaries_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"paired_sst_boundaries_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"width_descriptor_applies_to_every_winter_month\": false,\r\n        \"source_figures_digitized_for_this_descriptor\": false,\r\n        \"summer_50km_core_shift_is_width_change\": false,\r\n        \"core_offshore_distance_is_width\": false,\r\n        \"ngcuc_width_transferred\": false,\r\n        \"width_range_is_annual\": false,\r\n        \"source_cruise_season_label_conflict\": \"Section 2.2 pairs trade winds with Dec-Feb and northwest monsoon with Jun-Sep, opposite sections 1/5 narrative. These cruise labels are not used to date the width descriptors.\",\r\n        \"display_title\": \"Western widest sections / tracks 023 and 201\",\r\n        \"display_aria_label\": \"Western widest sections / tracks 023 and 201: approximately 200 km, author trade-wind surface current-anomaly vein descriptor. No midpoint, annual extrema, mapped edges or numerical uncertainty supplied.\",\r\n        \"display_caption\": \"Western widest sections / tracks 023 and 201: approximately 200 km. Trade-wind / austral-winter description, illustrated by August seasonal fields. Current-anomaly vein, not full-depth or instantaneous current width.\",\r\n        \"display_method_note\": \"2001–2010 seasonal climatology context; exact width dates, paired edges and uncertainty unresolved. Current descriptors share one source claim and overlap geographically; the near-200 km western maxima are a subset of the 100–200 km western span. Figure 3 variability-envelope widths, 80/340 km SLA smoothing, core displacement and offshore core position remain distinct metrics. No seasonal width animation inferred.\",\r\n        \"quality_note\": \"Complete unchanged HAL deposit inspected. Author regional numbers retained with their metrics and seasonal context; paired boundaries and numeric errors not recovered.\",\r\n        \"source_pdf_sha256\": \"