cal flow obliquity and ship track not reconstructed.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface and thermocline flow in neutral density layers 1-4 (gamma_n < 27.3800 kg/m3). Fixed depth bounds are not supplied.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Fall 2009. The 15 October-11 November dates bound the cruise; exact section occupation days remain unknown.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Published current-band coordinate limits; no independently digitized velocity cutoff or physical edge.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1002/jgrc.20227\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Perez-Hernandez et al. (2013), The source of the Canary current in fall 2009, JGR Oceans 118, 2874-2891.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Abstract; section6 paragraph32 and Figure14a; Table1; section7 paragraph40; section2 paragraph7.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-17\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"primary_fulltext_review_plus_frozen_local_source_coordinates_no_raw_pdf\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"WGS84 inverse geodesic between previously curated source limits; display rounded to nearest kilometre. No figure digitization.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"ORCA local section / fall 2009\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"campaign_coordinate_derived_section_span\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Source coordinate precision, datum, exact section dates, physical edges and obliquity remain unresolved. Cruise envelope is context only.\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Recover original PDF bytes and review page images.\",\r\n        \"Recover exact section dates, station coordinates, layer-specific physical boundary criterion and uncertainty.\",\r\n        \"Obtain compatible repeat sections before seasonal or annual comparison.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"published_section_context\": {\r\n        \"source_event_id\": \"orca-2009-portugal-north-section\",\r\n        \"source_event\": {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"portugal\",\r\n          \"observation_event_id\": \"orca-2009-portugal-north-section\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Portugal Current\",\r\n          \"state_code\": \"NAST E\",\r\n          \"reported_locality\": \"ORCA 37°N section, 14.8–13.5°W\",\r\n          \"observation_start\": \"2009-10-15\",\r\n          \"observation_end\": \"2009-11-11\",\r\n          \"observation_type\": \"hydrographic_section_and_inverse_box_model\",\r\n          \"time_detail\": \"The dates bound the entire ORCA cruise; the exact occupation dates of this current band are not separately assigned here.\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1002/jgrc.20227\",\r\n          \"source_locator\": \"Portugal Current discussion; 37°N ORCA section\",\r\n          \"spatial_basis\": \"The paper reports the Portugal Current between 14.8°W and 13.5°W along its 37°N section. This is a cross-stream band, not an along-current trace.\",\r\n          \"reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat\": [\r\n            [\r\n              -14.8,\r\n              37\r\n            ],\r\n            [\r\n              -13.5,\r\n              37\r\n            ]\r\n          ],\r\n          \"state_assignment_method\": \"source_reported_section_intersects_approximate_osw_state_polygon\",\r\n          \"state_boundary_limit\": \"The reported cross-stream band intersects the approximate NAST E polygon; the state boundary and observed current extent are not surveyed together.\",\r\n          \"physical_relation\": \"observed_local_cross_stream_section_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved\",\r\n          \"geometry_status\": \"source_re