quire review; no tracked annual current width or extrema. Separate 1995–2016 equal-year monthly climatology and 22 yearly monthly profiles per calendar month are also retained. Interannual spread is conditional on resolved sections, not uncertainty or physical annual width extrema.\",\r\n      \"sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"file\": \"research/south-indian-80e-2013-monthly-component-spans.json\",\r\n          \"sha256\": \"71242c8fe62379e4ed661dc2ad4a4ed4908aabc7558fe40ba715892883607346\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"file\": \"research/south-indian-80e-1995-2016-climatological-component-spans.json\",\r\n          \"sha256\": \"f777b7689328f47a352a597dd30004a8e25c494aa083aeda24bb94ac31dc39e8\"\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"aleutian\",\r\n      \"status\": \"local_component_section_diagnostic_requires_scientific_review\",\r\n      \"metric\": \"fixed_orientation_half_peak_eastward_component_span\",\r\n      \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"visual_url\": \"query.html?q=%7B%22collection%22%3A%22width_samples%22%2C%22filters%22%3A%5B%7B%22field%22%3A%22current_id%22%2C%22op%22%3A%22eq%22%2C%22value%22%3A%22aleutian%22%7D%5D%2C%22sort%22%3A%7B%22field%22%3A%22month%22%2C%22direction%22%3A%22asc%22%7D%2C%22limit%22%3A100%7D#query-chart-section\",\r\n      \"scope_note\": \"One 2013 local monthly-mean OSCAR component section. Current association and resolution require review; no tracked annual current width or extrema.\",\r\n      \"sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"file\": \"research/aleutian-160w-2013-monthly-component-spans.json\",\r\n          \"sha256\": \"e712741722e85ecf0155f5d140b44799d0f02abcea05c484f2ccc41044f5f34e\"\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"south-australian\",\r\n      \"status\": \"local_component_section_diagnostic_requires_scientific_review\",\r\n      \"metric\": \"fixed_orientation_half_peak_eastward_component_span\",\r\n      \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"visual_url\": \"query.html?q=%7B%22collection%22%3A%22width_samples%22%2C%22filters%22%3A%5B%7B%22field%22%3A%22current_id%22%2C%22op%22%3A%22eq%22%2C%22value%22%3A%22south-australian%22%7D%5D%2C%22sort%22%3A%7B%22field%22%3A%22month%22%2C%22direction%22%3A%22asc%22%7D%2C%22limit%22%3A100%7D#query-chart-section\",\r\n      \"scope_note\": \"One 2012 local monthly-mean HYCOM 100 m eastward-component section. Association and resolution require review; no tracked annual current width or extrema.\",\r\n      \"sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"file\": \"research/south-australian-132e-100m-2012-monthly-component-spans.json\",\r\n          \"sha256\": \"1a70cd4fdb8761b905c14ae7cce2419ae905a489c06421a57fbbd789f009e0e3\"\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coverage_counting_rule\": \"Counts follow exclusive current_decisions; source-specific pending candidates and reviews may coexist with scoped records.\"\r\n}\r\n"},"routes":{"source_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_sha256":"b06caed27655c39f8127ddda441cba0a856800f599ec52edcd5b30d2ad37b633","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-candidates.v1\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_candidates_not_canonical_length_admissions\",\r\n  \"counts\": {\r\n    \"currents_without_published_ranked_estimate\": 89,\r\n    \"currents_with_route_candidates\": 70,\r\n    \"currents_without_route_candidates\": 19,\r\n    \"route_candidates\": 76,\r\n    \"studied_reach_candidates\": 37\r\n  },\r\n  \"comparison_rule\": \"Descending length of declared OSW reference routes only. Coherent jets, specified branches and source/region-defined extents differ in scope; their order is provisional and is not a uniform whole-current ranking. Studied reaches are excluded from the reference-route order. No number replaces the existing length evidence or published ranking.\",\r\n  \"reference_route_length_order\": [\r\n    \"north-pacific-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"labrador-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"canary-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"alaska-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"irminger-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"oyashio-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"algerian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"zeehan-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"gaspe-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"jutland-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"length_evidence_sha256\": \"c9860385231435451fdd1c989342dc73fd45ce4ac774be1a10c14576b4dfc3fc\",\r\n  \"planning_taxonomy\": {\r\n    \"status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n    \"author\": \"OSW\",\r\n    \"scope\": \"Primary construction strategy for each of the 89 inventory names without a published ranked length. Categories are work priorities, can have overlapping physical constraints, and do not establish current boundaries or comparable lengths.\",\r\n    \"input_file\": \"research/ocean-current-route-strategy-input.json\",\r\n    \"input_sha256\": \"f1b33c151b22ff56d80db60113403e6090accfb903c372048ab4cbfd9dce6036\",\r\n    \"current_ledger_sha256\": \"6c8a143208c0953512875f222154a819d5f56b7326daa6816f0609e61b4f261e\",\r\n    \"parent_taxonomy\": \"research/ocean-motion-taxonomy.json\",\r\n    \"strategies\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"split_basin_family\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Split basin families\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Shared labels need basin-specific child objects before any route length. Existing children are navigation links, not a complete family census.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 8,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 8\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"system_route_graph\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Define system and branch graph\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A main route, component reaches and alternate branches need separate length semantics.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 3,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 2\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"continuity_hypothesis\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Keep continuity hypothesis separate\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A proposed connection cannot be ranked as an established current merely because a path can be drawn.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Audit continuity evidence and alternatives; retain hypothetical status and any proposed distance separately.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 1,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"seasonal_routes\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct seasonal routes\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A specified seasonal regime is needed; reversal or seasonal extensions cannot become a permanent route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 14,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 2\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"dated_geometry\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Variable loops, circuits and frontal paths need a specified date or regime and continuity test.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Use dated or explicitly averaged geometry, distinguish an open loop from a closed circuit, and compare repeated regimes before summarizing.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 3,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"resolve_naming_scope\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Resolve naming or extent convention\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Aliases, source-dependent limits or proposed continuity need an explicit identity/extent decision. A regional candidate may use a declared convention meanwhile.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 16,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 4\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Subsurface jets, undercurrents and overflows require depth, density or tracer support along the route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 13,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"expand_section_evidence\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Extend evidence beyond sections\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Cross-stream sections locate a current locally but do not define an along-stream route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Find sourced upstream/downstream gates and continuity between sections; preserve widths and section transports as different measurements.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 5,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"preserve_survey_reach\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Preserve surveyed-reach scope\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A documented regional survey reach remains a reach until whole-flow gates are supported.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 1,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Regional named flow or branch eligible for a declared reference convention once gates and route geography are supported. This does not assert that the flow is unbranched or steady.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 25,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  \"candidates\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 5000,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        4900,\r\n        5000\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2 and 3; Figure 2b caption: BRAN monthly climatology, density-layer context and approximate 60-105 E reach shifting from 8 S to 10 S. Figure 3 core threshold is a separate diagnostic.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"09e20729d63ef0930ba1835f95fdc24285726de590f4d2c9915604358867c117\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"AUSW\",\r\n        \"EAFR\",\r\n        \"IND W\",\r\n        \"MONS\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_E_4\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Extract compatible BRAN density-layer core geometry and review ridge-scale continuity before interpreting the connecting line as an axis.\",\r\n        \"Resolve source latitude typo (10 N in one paragraph versus 8-10 S elsewhere); southern context is used explicitly.\",\r\n        \"Review endpoint definitions and extensions before whole-current length.\",\r\n        \"Recover repeated matched axes and core boundaries before annual length/width extrema or seasonal playback.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"parent_current_id\": null,\r\n      \"parent_scope_note\": null,\r\n      \"ordering_sensitivity\": null\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared east-central Pacific study reach from 140 W to 95 W. Gates truncate a larger current; western Pacific inflow and coastal redistribution east of 95 W are excluded. Intermediate bends are editorial connections among section descriptions, not a reconstructed continuous axis or parcel trajectory.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"140 W to 95 W study reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 5000,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        4900,\r\n        5100\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.1: 140 W near-surface core around 7 N, 125 W around 8 N, southward shift at 110 W and northward rebuilding at 95 W; section 3.2.3 separates seasonal surface expression near 110 W.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/data.shtml\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Johnson et al. (2002), section 2, Data and fitting.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"172 sections June 1985-December 2000, ten nominal longitude lines; ADCP mapping and annual-harmonic/SOI fitting.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Sampling and transformation context; does not date the editorial route.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"0df217ce291f5e8d4804a2fa25f86a2bb8a6fdd5101f00abe2401583ec00df01\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"CAMR\",\r\n        \"PEQD\",\r\n        \"PNEC\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_A_3\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review editor-selected 110 W/95 W latitudes and interpolating continuity against compatible velocity fields.\",\r\n        \"Extract depth and month-specific axes before length or width seasonal ranges.\",\r\n        \"Keep weak or absent surface flow near 110 W separate from subsurface eastward flow; no annual continuous path inferred.\",\r\n        \"Resolve western inflow and coastal redistribution separately from this truncated studied reach.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"parent_current_id\": null,\r\n      \"parent_scope_note\": null,\r\n      \"ordering_sensitivity\": null\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared northern Tsuchiya Jet studied reach from the 155 W mean-section core to the 110 W mean-section core. Western formation and basin continuation east of 110 W are excluded. The section gates truncate a larger current; interpolating bends are editor-selected, not a measured continuous centerline or particle path.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W northern Tsuchiya reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 5000,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        4900,\r\n        5100\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: north SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 N/220 m and 110 W 4.5 N/130 m. Transport integration latitude limits and 700-dbar reference are separately defined; they are not route width or a uniform axis layer.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Johnson et al. (2002), Direct measurements of upper ocean currents and water properties across the tropical Pacific during the 1990s.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Section 3.1: northern subsurface countercurrent/Tsuchiya name; 140 W around 4 N/200 m; eastward shoaling and mean/synoptic differences.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Later naming and layer context; not an additional dated or uniform-depth route.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"0afb68c180bb6a8528173974c6a88641f1f0a22ddc1db5683ee1f95c68760c33\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"PEQD\",\r\n        \"PNEC\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_A