elibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/2017JC013553\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Introduction and Figure 1: Atlantic flow splits between Scandinavia and Svalbard into Barents inflow via Bear Island Trough and northward WSC continuation; shelf/slope components differ.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1029/2018JC014299\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Menze et al. (2019), Atlantic Water Pathways Along the North-Western Svalbard Shelf Mapped Using Vessel-Mounted Current Profilers, JGR Oceans, doi:10.1029/2018JC014299.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Abstract; sections 4.3 and 6: northward boundary flow at 79-80 N / 5-10 E, splitting into Svalbard, Yermak and Yermak Pass branches.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Northern branch-region context; summer composite does not establish all branches at every time.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/1003/2026/\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Dundas and Fer (2026), Atlantic Water flow through Fram Strait to the Arctic Ocean measured by repeated glider transects, Ocean Science 22, 1003-1021.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Introduction; sections 2.1-2.2 and code/data availability: separate slope/front branches, 77.25 N target section and limited season coverage.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Source-specific naming and section/season caveats; transect distances are not current length or width.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"cd6c83f417d6aa8c73303be20ad3d2472f67769c43141e08e6619ca5b996fdfa\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"BPLR\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \