e solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2006GL026965\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"deep western boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"system_route_graph\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Define system and branch graph\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-adriatic\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Adriatic Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"northwestward coastal boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"resolve_naming_scope\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Resolve naming or extent convention\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-australian\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Australian Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marin