astal-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"low-salinity inner-shelf coastal jet\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"preserve_survey_reach\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Preserve surveyed-reach scope\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-greenland\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Greenland Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"polar boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Umbrella label for multiple eastward tropical countercurrents. North and South named families and basin-specific flows require separate boundaries and length estimates.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"reference_path_not_constructed\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n  