 North Atlantic Current. The whole system extends beyond the Grand Banks toward the British Isles, so no 3,000 km Florida-to-Grand-Banks span is treated as its complete length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"reference_path_not_constructed\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"multi-segment current system\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"system_route_graph\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Define system and branch graph\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"NOAA's glossary defines a continuous system comprising the Florida Current, Gulf Stream, and North Atlantic Current. The whole system extends beyond the Grand Banks toward the British Isles, so no 3,000 km Florida-to-Grand-Banks span is treated as its complete length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"florida\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Florida Current\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"gulf-stream\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Gulf Stream\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"known_component_records_not_complete_census\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"hiri-current\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Hiri Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The literature uses Hiri Current for the northward branch after South Equatorial Current bifurcation off northeast Australia, with variable continuation around the Gulf of Papua. No one fixed path or endpoint pair is admitted for a whole-current length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1002/2013JC009591\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"hiri-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"northward western boundary branch and Gulf of Papua circulation\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"resolve_naming_scope\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Resolve naming or extent convention\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The literature uses Hiri Current for the northward branch after South Equatorial Current bifurcation off northeast Australia, with variable continuation around the Gulf of Papua. No one fixed path or endpoint pair is admitted for a whole-current length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian Ocean Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"section_only\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Observed across a 2°S–2°N section at 90°E on 1–3 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"seasonal eastward subsurface jet\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"seasonal_routes\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct seasonal routes\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"Observed across a 2°S–2°N section at 90°E on 1–3 March 2017; the reported ~13.5 Sv is section transport, not path length. A later review describes the Indian expression as weaker and seasonally varying; one campaign does not establish a permanent path.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Repeated XBT shipping-line sections identify this flow, including a western line near 55°E with a variable trough around 5–10°S. Section transports and latitude bands are not