h and depth. That observed seasonal envelope is not a traced alongstream length and is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Recover compatible numerical total-flow axes and paired boundaries; keep WOA01 surface/0-200 m geostrophy relative to 1500 dbar separate from modeled Sverdrup flow and band-passed anomaly sections at 170 E. Do not use anomaly zero contours as width edges, averaging windows as endpoints, or merge them with the newer Argo envelopes. See research/pacific-secc-woa01-anomaly-scope-audit.json; full 2026 methods and seasonal calendars remain needed.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The Pacific 140°W section resolves two south-side branches near 4.5°S at 200 m and 7°S at 250 m. These section positions do not supply a whole-current path length or a single branch-averaged centerline.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"eastward subsurface jets south of the Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classificatio