        [\r\n                13.25,\r\n                45\r\n              ]\r\n            ]\r\n          },\r\n          \"role\": \"editorial_reference_route\",\r\n          \"note\": \"OSW offshore eastern-Adriatic reference corridor under the Otranto-to-Istria surface-circulation convention. Gates are editorial neighborhoods, not observed origins or termination. Excludes western return flow, sub-basin recirculation loops and unverified island-channel branches. The possible Dalmatian-name overlap is unresolved and its extent is not transferred. The published 800 km basin length is not used as current length; this estimate comes from the declared OSW vertices.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\r\n      \"connections\": [],\r\n      \"scope_notes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-adriatic\",\r\n          \"label\": \"East Adriatic naming and extent convention\",\r\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/east-adriatic-naming-extent-scope-audit.json\",\r\n          \"summary\": \"Eastern-coast northwestward circulation convention is distinct from the western return and basin gyres. Otranto-to-Istria context is not a diagnosed whole-current axis; Dalmatian-name overlap remains unresolved, and 800 km basin length is not current length.\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/\",\r\n          \"source_locator\": \"Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern-coast EAC, separate southeastward western-coast WAC, three sub-basin recirculations, wind modulation.\",\r\n          \"observed_period\": null\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"evidence_links\": [],\r\n      \"object_url\": \"object.html?id=current%3Aeast-adriatic\",\r\n      \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"season_url\": \"seasons.html?current=east-adriatic\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"current:east-australian\",\r\n      \"label\": \"East Australi