hflow-network-input.json\",\r\n          \"summary\": \"Selected western/eastern inflow and three main exit pathways represented as twelve conceptual nodes and fourteen connections. Three exit transport means retain 2004–2006 support, processing-choice intervals and eight published first-deployment mooring positions. No geographic network edges, full system length, current width, annual extrema or instantaneous one-way-flow claim.\",\r\n          \"observed_period\": {\r\n            \"start_year\": 2004,\r\n            \"end_year\": 2006,\r\n            \"precision\": \"year\"\r\n          },\r\n          \"source_time_caution\": \"Abstract mentions January 2003; Table 1 explicitly reports 2004–2006 averages. Individual mooring deployment dates differ, including an August 2003 Ombai deployment. Preserve these distinctions.\",\r\n          \"integration_width_caution\": \"35/35/160 km are transport-integration widths, not current widths. Ombai geographic width is discussed as 37 km in paragraph 8, while transport calculations use 35 km. Neither provides a uniform current footprint.\",\r\n          \"whole_current_length_km\": null,\r\n          \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n          \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n          \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n          \"rank_eligible\": false,\r\n          \"canonical_taxonomy_admitted\": false,\r\n          \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n            \"Assess full passage/depth coverage and reversals; no complete network asserted.\",\r\n            \"Recover axes and scientifically justify branch gates before measuring lengths.\",\r\n            \"Keep upstream and downstream transport budgets separate; no sum over graph edges.\",\r\n            \"Review original processing and observation gaps before new derived dimensions.\"\r\n          ]\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"schema\": \"osw.current-measurement-object-scope.v1\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indonesian-throughflow\",\r\n          \