rent centerline or endpoint.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"geometry\": {\r\n            \"type\": \"LineString\",\r\n            \"coordinates\": [\r\n              [\r\n                146,\r\n                -3.5\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                145,\r\n                -3\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                144,\r\n                -2.5\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                143,\r\n                -2\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                142,\r\n                -1.5\r\n              ]\r\n            ]\r\n          },\r\n          \"role\": \"editorial_reference_route\",\r\n          \"note\": \"Declared 146 E to 142 E offshore north-New-Guinea surface reference reach, ordered northwestward for the trade-wind convention. Both gates and every vertex are selected by OSW. Excludes southeast coastal continuation, Vitiaz Strait, Halmahera branches and the deeper New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent; not a whole-current endpoint or observed axis.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\r\n      \"connections\": [],\r\n      \"scope_notes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n          \"label\": \"Local seasonal direction and El Niño exception\",\r\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/new-guinea-coastal-current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.json\",\r\n          \"summary\": \"Local upper-ocean direction composite reverses southeastward November–April to northwestward May–October. Three-cycle sampling, gaps and El Niño exceptions limit annual interpretation. Direction symbols are not current axes or measured seasonal lengths/widths.\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242\",\r\n          \"source_locator\": \"Data and Method, sections 3.2–3.3 / Figures 4 and 9 captions\",\r\n          \"observed_period\": null,\r\n          \"related_current_ids\": [\