,\r\n                -6.8\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                157,\r\n                -5.8\r\n              ],\r\n              [\r\n                155.8,\r\n                -4.6\r\n              ]\r\n            ]\r\n          },\r\n          \"role\": \"editorial_reference_route\",\r\n          \"note\": \"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\r\n      \"connections\": [],\r\n      \"scope_notes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"label\": \"Model proposal, later regional observations and editorial reach\",\r\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-proposal-scope-audit.json\",\r\n          \"summary\": \"The 2010 model proposes SICU east of the Solomon Islands. A pinned 2017 primary paper interprets northward flow near northeast Bougainville, with ADCP and tracer station context. OSW adds an offshore geographic reference reach; continuous measured axis, complete endpoints, width and annual ranges remain unresolved.\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html\",\r\n          \"source_locator\": \"Author-hosted abstract: previously unknown current east of Solomon Sea formed where SEC meets Solomon Islands; named Solomon Islands Coastal Undercurrent.\",\r\n          \"observed_period\": null,\r\n          \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n            {\r\n              \"label\": \"Ganachaud et al. (2017), Solomon Sea cruises\",\r\n              \"url\": \"ht