 not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\r\n      \"connections\": [],\r\n      \"scope_notes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-indian\",\r\n          \"label\": \"Eastern naming convention and idealized transport reach\",\r\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/south-indian-eastern-reach-naming-layer-scope-audit.json\",\r\n          \"summary\": \"70–90 E is a declared regional reach under the eastern SIOC naming convention. Longitude gates are approximate context, and every latitude/connecting bend is editorial. Historical upper-1000 m transport is not a fixed-depth axis; western ARC, recirculation and northeastern continuation are not summed. Whole-current and annual dimensions remain unresolved.\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455\",\r\n          \"source_locator\": \"Stramma and Lutjeharms (1997) section 3.2; Grand et al. (2015) section 3.1.1; earlier/later naming conventions retained.\",\r\n          \"observed_period\": null,\r\n          \"related_current_ids\": [\r\n            \"agulhas-return\"\r\n          ]\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"evidence_links\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"label\": \"Why physical width remains unresolved\",\r\n          \"url\": \"query.html?source-q=%7B%22document%22%3A%20%22research/southern-current-width-source-limitations-audit.json%22%2C%20%22pointer%22%3A%20%22/reviews/0%22%2C%20%22limit%22%3A%20100%7D\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"label\": \"Monthly section profiles and resolution flags\",\r\n          \"url\": \"../figures/south-indian-80e-2013-monthly-component-profiles.svg\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"label\": \"1995–2016 calendar-month climatology at 80 E profiles\",\r\n        